.TH "ST\-WL\-COPY" "1" "January 2020" "secure-terminal" "secure-terminal Manual"
.SH "NAME"
\fBst\-wl\-copy\fR \- wl\-copy that sanitizes the clipboard on write
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBst\-wl\-copy\fR [\fIWL\-COPY\-OPTION\fR\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
st\-wl\-copy is a drop\-in replacement for \fBwl\-copy\fR(1) (Wayland) that filters standard input through \fBsclip\fR(1) before it is placed on the clipboard\. Every argument is forwarded verbatim to \fBwl\-copy\fR, so native options such as \fB\-\-primary\fR or \fB\-\-trim\-newline\fR work unchanged\.
.P
By default the strip is strictest (printable ASCII only)\. Set the environment variable \fBSCLIP_MODE=unicode\fR to keep printable non\-ASCII instead\.
.P
A TEXT OPERAND (\fBwl\-copy some text\fR) is REFUSED (exit 2): wl\-copy copies a text operand directly and ignores standard input, so the operand would reach the clipboard unsanitized\. Pipe the text instead (\fBprintf %s 'some text' | st\-wl\-copy\fR)\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBSCLIP_MODE\fR
When set to \fBunicode\fR, keep printable non\-ASCII (passes \fB\-\-unicode\fR to \fBsclip\fR)\. Any other value (or unset) is the default ASCII\-only strip\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
The exit status of the underlying \fBsclip\fR | \fBwl\-copy\fR pipeline; 127 if \fBwl\-copy\fR is not installed\.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBst\-wl\-paste\fR(1), \fBst\-xclip\fR(1), \fBsclip\fR(1), \fBwl\-copy\fR(1)
